    {
      "name": "create_access_key",
      "description": "Create a narrower access key to hand to a subagent or another tool. If you are using an access key, the new key is its child: it can never do more than your key (enforced by the database on every request) and revoking your key revokes it. If you are connected through OAuth (e.g. the Claude connector), the new key is independent: it is limited only by the scope you set, and it is NOT revoked with your connection — it expires on its own or via revoke_access_key. A subagent only stays inside the key if it is given this key INSTEAD of your connection (see docs/MCP.md). Capabilities: read < comment < propose < edit (each includes the previous); manage (rename/archive), share, admin are separate.",
      "inputSchema": {
        "type": "object",
        "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
